<section class="blk blk--first">
  <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
  <h1>We’re early. Here’s exactly how early.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Uncost is a nonprofit, nonpartisan movement working to lower the real cost of living using evidence, AI, robotics and open tools. It is also, right now, very new — so here is the honest state of it.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">What exists today</p>
  <h2 class="sec">What exists today.</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A published method and movement plan.</li>
    <li>Fifteen sector dossiers.</li>
    <li>Ten draft policies and seven project briefs, all public and open to criticism.</li>
    <li>A public repository anyone can inspect.</li>
    <li>A public source register, carrying its first verified entries — we’d rather show you a short, sourced shelf than a long one we can’t back up.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">What doesn’t exist yet</p>
  <h2 class="sec">What doesn’t exist yet.</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We are not incorporated.</li>
    <li>We have no fiscal sponsor confirmed.</li>
    <li>We cannot accept donations.</li>
    <li>The Assembly is not operating.</li>
    <li>The dashboard is designed, not built.</li>
    <li>No policy on this site is in force — every one is a draft awaiting review.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">Why we say all that here</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Why we say all that on the About page.</h2>
  <p>Because the entire method rests on showing our work. A movement that hides its own status has no business asking you to trust its numbers.</p>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--ink">
  <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
  <h2 class="sec">How a cost gets uncosted.</h2>
  <p class="lead">Six steps. No magic. The whole method is public, and so is every step we get wrong.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Measure what it really costs, from public data.</li>
    <li>Show every source before the conclusions.</li>
    <li>Find what drives the cost.</li>
    <li>Identify what could lower it — counting what it adds as well as what it saves.</li>
    <li>Package it so others can build and run it.</li>
    <li>Track whether it worked — and publish the answer either way.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="eyebrow">Plainly</p>
  <h2 class="sec">What Uncost is — and is not.</h2>
  <h3>Uncost is</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>A nonprofit, nonpartisan movement to lower the real cost of living.</li>
    <li>Evidence-first — every public number carries its source, its date, and the region it covers.</li>
    <li>Open — methods, models, and tools are public and reusable wherever rights, safety, and privacy allow.</li>
    <li>Advisory — supporters get a structured, recorded say, within legal, fiduciary, and safeguarding limits.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Uncost is not</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>A political party or candidate campaign.</li>
    <li>A crypto, DAO, or token project.</li>
    <li>A promise that every physical constraint disappears or that everything becomes free.</li>
    <li>A replacement for local democratic control or qualified professional judgment.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="blk blk--cream2">
  <p class="eyebrow">Who runs it</p>
  <h2 class="sec">Who runs Uncost.</h2>
  <p>Founder-led, with an advisory group forming. Sector and region leads are being recruited. We’ll name people when there are people to name — not before.</p>
</section>

